# GFM Cloaked Project Rules

## Architecture
- Two-domain system: campaign servers (per language) + multi-tenant store server
- Campaign NEVER touches Stripe directly, all payments go through the store
- Store configs live in Supabase `stores` table, not in code
- Campaign content lives in JSON files under `campaign/campaigns/`

## Critical Security
- NEVER log or expose Stripe secret keys in console output or error messages
- Referrer-Policy is `strict-origin-when-cross-origin` globally (browser default for ecommerce)
- The ONLY place `no-referrer` is used is in the meta-refresh HTML at `/s/:token` (breaks campaign→store referrer chain)
- NEVER add campaign identifiers to Stripe metadata
- Donor session cookie MUST be httpOnly
- Token expiry MUST be 5 minutes or less
- NEVER use donation-related terminology in ANY code that touches Stripe (no "donation", "donor", "campaign", "fundraiser")
- NEVER add micro-variance to decomposed product prices (Stripe silently drops L2/L3 data when arithmetic doesn't match)
- NEVER use `payment_method_types`; always use `automatic_payment_methods: { enabled: true, allow_redirects: 'never' }`
- NEVER use `?donated=true` or any donation-revealing query parameters; use `?status=complete`

## Database
- Supabase project: "DB for Projects" (wzialsfdguuircomaqvp)
- Service role key in env vars, never hardcoded
- Triggers auto-update customer_totals and store_stats
- Weighted store selection via `get_next_store()` RPC: each `stores` row carries `weight_pct` (0-100), and the RPC picks the active store whose current month-to-date revenue share is furthest below its target weight (deficit-fill). Active store weights should sum to 100; `status` is binary `active|paused`.

## Store Frontend
- EJS templates with Tailwind CSS (CDN)
- Colors driven by CSS variables from store config
- All pages must render with store name/branding from DB
- checkout-donor.ejs = minimal form (donors), checkout-store.ejs = full store (reviewers)

## PaymentIntent Requirements
- `automatic_payment_methods: { enabled: true }` (not manual payment_method_types)
- `payment_details.order_reference` = reference code (required for L2/L3)
- `amount_details.tax.total_tax_amount` = 0 (required for L2/L3)
- `amount_details.line_items[]` = decomposed product items (exact sum must equal PaymentIntent amount)
- Store-specific metadata key names (different per store to avoid cross-store pattern detection)
- Fulfillment evidence updated post-payment (delivered/digital_download)

## Conventions
- No comments in code
- Use Supabase MCP tools for database changes
- Campaign server: port 3000, Store server: port 4000
- All amounts in database are decimal (not cents)
- Stripe amounts are in cents (multiply by 100)

## Template & Style Sharing
- HTML/CSS template structure CAN be shared between stores safely
- Color scheme (CSS colors) CAN be shared — Stripe compares text content, not visual design
- All stores and campaign share the same green (#00b964) palette and Inter font
- Stripe compares semantic content (product names, descriptions, about text), NOT code/template structure
- Millions of Shopify/SamCart/WooCommerce merchants share identical templates
- Only CONTENT must differ per store: product names, descriptions, about text, reviews, contact email, store name

## Account Isolation (Per Account Burn)
- MUST rotate on burn: Stripe account, domain, AdsPower profile, residential IP, store name, product content, about text, contact email, statement descriptor, metadata key names (NOT color scheme)
- Safe to reuse: HTML/CSS templates, JS logic, Supabase DB, Railway hosting IPs, decompose logic, Tailwind CSS, page structure
- See docs/ACCOUNT-ISOLATION.md for the full checklist

## Failed Approaches (Don't Repeat These)
- Micro-variance on line item prices: Stripe dropped ALL L2/L3 data when sum ≠ total
- `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` globally: unusual for ecommerce, potential detection signal
- `?donated=true` redirect param: leaks donation context in URL
- Manual `payment_method_types: ['card', 'link']`: limits payment options, less natural
- `automatic_payment_methods` without `allow_redirects: 'never'`: redirect methods error with no `return_url`
- Missing `unit_of_measure: 'ACT'` on line items: only L2 qualification, not L3
- Assuming HTML/CSS templates must differ per store: they don't, only content matters
